WEBVTT

00:00:01.850 --> 00:00:06.554
For over a year, I've run a Monday night figure drawing session at Enoch's, a coffee shop in New York.

00:00:08.350 --> 00:00:12.460
Every Monday after the session, I'd text next week's model to re-confirm.

00:00:12.816 --> 00:00:15.446
And all week, models wrote in to swap dates.

00:00:15.446 --> 00:00:16.522
All of it by hand.

00:00:17.283 --> 00:00:22.113
So I built Posebook: models manage their own schedule, and it does the reminding.

00:00:22.883 --> 00:00:24.445
I set the session up once:

00:00:24.816 --> 00:00:26.165
Mondays at six-thirty.

00:00:26.916 --> 00:00:30.138
Models I've invited pick an open Monday and book it themselves.

00:00:30.516 --> 00:00:34.920
They swap or cancel on their own, and confirm with one tap: I'll be there!

00:00:35.683 --> 00:00:39.793
My calendar shows who's posing each week, and who has confirmed.

00:00:40.550 --> 00:00:45.531
Posebook asks next week's model to confirm, and reminds them before the session.

00:00:45.883 --> 00:00:48.525
And my Google Calendar is managed automatically.

00:00:49.283 --> 00:00:50.821
Posebook is open source.

00:00:50.821 --> 00:00:52.743
Run it for your drawing group.

00:00:53.516 --> 00:00:58.438
And if you're in New York, come draw with us: Mondays at six-thirty, at Enoch's.
